[0m┌ CORE CONCEPTS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐[179C[0;1m^[0m
[0m│ [0;38;5;189;1mMEMORY      [0mThe basic record unit stored inside a Context and independently selected, reviewed, or changed by Memory-level operations.                                          [0m│[179C[0;48;5;238m [0m
[0m│ [0;1mCONTEXT     [0mA named hierarchical workspace that contains Memories and organizes child Contexts. The / separator expresses hierarchy in names such as task-1/participant;        [0m│[179C[0;48;5;238m [0m
[0m│             operations with descendant scope can treat a Context and its descendant Contexts as one subtree. Commands use the current Context when none is specified.           [0m│[179C[0;48;5;238m [0m
[0m│ [0;1mPROFILE     [0mAn isolated ownership and storage boundary containing Contexts; different Profiles may contain the same Context name.                                               [0m│[179C[0;48;5;238m [0m
[0m│ [0;1mOPERATION   [0mA reusable action that reads, analyzes, or changes selected Memories or Contexts through defined inputs and behavior.                                               [0m│[179C[0;48;5;238m [0m
[0m│ [0;1mGRANT       [0mA permission relationship that can be given or received, selectively allowing someone without direct ownership to read or query a Context and its Memories, or run  [0m│[179C[0;48;5;238m [0m
[0m│             permitted operations on them, while the Grant remains valid.                                                                                                        [0m│[179C[0;48;5;238m [0m
[0m│ [0;1mSESSION     [0mStores an analysis or review workflow so it can be reopened and continued. Apply results and checkpoint history separately show whether Context changes were made.  [0m│[179C[0;48;5;238m [0m
[0m│ [0;1mCHECKPOINT  [0mA recoverable history boundary created for each applied operation and recorded per affected Context.                                                                [0m│[179C[0;48;5;238m [0m
[0m├ COMMON LOCATORS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤[179C[0;48;5;248m [0m
[0m│ [0;1mNAME         [0mA bare existing Context name is canonical and global, never relative.                                                                                              [0m│[179C[0;48;5;248m [0m
[0m│ [0;1m.            [0mThe current Context captured once when the command starts.                                                                                                         [0m│[179C[0;48;5;248m [0m
[0m│ [0;1m..           [0mThe parent of that captured current Context.                                                                                                                       [0m│[179C[0;48;5;248m [0m
[0m│ [0;1m./CHILD      [0mA child path relative to that captured current Context.                                                                                                            [0m│[179C[0;48;5;248m [0m
[0m│ [0;1m../PATH      [0mA path relative to the parent of that captured current Context.                                                                                                    [0m│[179C[0;48;5;248m [0m
[0m│ [0;1mUID          [0mA full UID or accepted prefix. In supported direct-Memory operations, scan ordinary local Contexts; exactly one direct owner must match, or ambiguity stops and    [0m│[179C[0;48;5;248m [0m
[0m│              lists qualified candidates.                                                                                                                                        [0m│[179C[0;48;5;248m [0m
[0m│ [0;1mCONTEXT:UID  [0mIn supported direct-Memory operations, : separates the direct owner Context from its Memory UID or prefix; the Context may be relative, as in ../3:ca562047.       [0m│[179C[0;48;5;248m [0m
